# The CI jobs, one per line: `<id> <linux> <script> [args...]`.
#
#   <script>  scripts/ci/<script>.sh, run with [args...].
#   <linux>   `gate` or `advisory`: whether a Linux failure fails CI. On macOS
#             every job gates. The advisory jobs fail on Linux today because
#             the Linux HTTP client does not stream (design/linux.md); they
#             still run, so the gap stays visible, and move to `gate` when it
#             is closed. Conformance baselines and interop/RESULTS.md are
#             shared by both platforms.
#
# `scripts/ci-linux.sh all` runs every line; .github/workflows/ci.yml runs the
# same scripts with the same arguments.
build-test                     gate      build-test
docs                           gate      docs
conformance-scripts            gate      conformance-scripts
conformance-2025-11-25-client  advisory  conformance --spec-version 2025-11-25 --mode client
conformance-2025-11-25-server  gate      conformance --spec-version 2025-11-25 --mode server
conformance-2026-07-28-client  gate      conformance --spec-version 2026-07-28 --mode client
conformance-2026-07-28-server  gate      conformance --spec-version 2026-07-28 --mode server
conformance-default-client     advisory  conformance --mode client
conformance-default-server     gate      conformance --mode server
tier-2025-11-25-client         advisory  conformance --requirements 2025-11-25 --mode client
tier-2025-11-25-server         gate      conformance --requirements 2025-11-25 --mode server
tier-2026-07-28-client         gate      conformance --requirements 2026-07-28 --mode client
tier-2026-07-28-server         gate      conformance --requirements 2026-07-28 --mode server
interop                        advisory  interop --check
